  <running_head>Institutionum</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">§. 3. Ex his aliquid licebit facile</l>
    <l n="2">judicare de quibusdam particularibus</l>
    <l n="3">controversiis, <i>qua inter partes viventis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>corporis veniant numeranda?</i> Uti 1. <i>An</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>humor nutritivus, v. g. in animalibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>perfectis fanguis, &amp; spiritus influens ei in-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>existens sint partes?</i> Sane non sunt par-</l>
    <l n="8">tes ipsius corporis, quippe ad ejus</l>
    <l n="9">quantitatem integrandam non confe-</l>
    <l n="10">runt, neque ad compositionem ejus</l>
    <l n="11">pertinent: forte tamen sunt partes to-</l>
    <l n="12">tius, quatenus in illis dependenter &amp;</l>
    <l n="13">conservative anima fundatur: quae pri-</l>
    <l n="14">mo calido innato &amp; humido radicali</l>
    <l n="15">innititur. 2. <i>An pars partis, v. g. frag-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>mentum ossis, portio cordis vel radicis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>etiam partium nomine venire debeant?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">Distinguendum est. Sunt enim partes</l>
    <l n="19">secundum definitionem generalem par-</l>
    <l n="20">tis integrantis: verum non sunt partes</l>
    <l n="21">secundum definitionem partis inte-</l>
    <l n="22">grantis specialem. Nam in illa valet</l>
    <l n="23">regula: <i>pars partis est etiam pars totius:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">in hac limitationem postulat taliter:</l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>pars partis integrantis dissimilaris est</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>etiam pars aut portio aut particula totius.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" type="heading" level="2" para="true">XXI. <i>In partibus, ut debite se ha-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>beant, requiritur conveniens habitudo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>proprietatum corporis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30" para="true">XXII. <i>Sunt ea in omnibus conve-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="31">
      <i>niens</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
